        ":question/problem": "Given that $y = -\\frac{29}{10}\\ln x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{29}{10}\\ln x) \\\\ & =-\\frac{29}{10}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\ & =-\\frac{29}{10}\\cdot\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ & =-\\frac{29}{10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
